# What the lakeshore pays for its water and weather (M51), measured
# in-process (see README, Measuring performance). Each bench is "off on"
# (rain "0 1"), so the reported B - A is the cost; "weather" is water and
# rain together. Two views: from the beach across the shallows, and from
# the jetty's end out over open water.
#
#   ATOM_VSYNC=0 ATOM_START_LEVEL=lakeshore ATOM_TEST_SCRIPT=Tools/Perf/water_and_weather.atomtest AtomGame.exe
#
# v0.0.8, laptop plugged in (Iris Xe, 1280x720, Balanced power plan), two
# runs, median paired deltas:
#                 beach            jetty's end
#   water         +0.340 / +0.331  +0.685 / +0.681 ms
#   rain          +0.253 / +0.208  +0.163 / +0.191 ms
#   weather       +0.600 / +0.663  +0.889 / +0.933 ms
# Water costs with the screen it covers (per pixel: noise, Fresnel, sky);
# rain is mostly its 1,400 drops (CPU update, sort, upload) and their
# overdraw. Together under 1 ms at worst: affordable, nothing to optimise.
#   reflection    +0.201 / +0.217  +0.121 / +0.150 ms
# The planar reflection (an experiment, kept): the opaque near scene
# mirrored at half resolution; the lakeshore's draws are few.
timeout 600
wait 2
teleport -3 0.25 -2 20                # the beach
wait 1
bench water off on 8 2
bench rain 0 1 8 2
bench weather off on 8 2
bench reflection off on 8 2
teleport 0 0.5 -16 0                  # the jetty's end
wait 1
bench water off on 8 2
bench rain 0 1 8 2
bench weather off on 8 2
bench reflection off on 8 2
quit
